      "title": "Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fd217f80-a23c-5137-9286-a58eb76c157f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "If\n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3x & -2 \\\\ 6x & x+6\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(D)=-75$, what is the value of $x?$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3x & -2 \\\\ 6x & x+6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3x\\cdot (x+6)-(-2)\\cdot 6x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+30x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-75$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-75 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+30x & =-75 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+30x+75 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+10x+25 & =0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
